<div class="guide-styles" data-zaf-dynamic="article" id="guide-body" lang="en">Welcome to Wowhead's Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear list for <span class="c2">
<span class="icontiny" style='background-image: url("https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_auraoflight.gif");'>Retribution Paladin</span></span> DPS in Cataclysm Classic Phase 2. This guide will list the recommended gear for your class and role, containing gear sourced from dungeons, PvP, professions, Bind on Equip drops, and reputations.<h2 class="heading-size-2" id="pre-raid-best-in-slot">
<span class="c2">Pre-Raid Best in Slot Gear for Retribution Paladin DPS in Phase 2</span></h2>Paladins will focus primarily on melee damage-dealing statistics like Strength, Hit, Expertise, Mastery, Critical Strike, and Haste. You will need to reach the cap for hit chance and expertise to ensure that your attacks are not dodged or miss, causing a loss of potential Holy Power and damage.<ol>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Hit Rating</b> - The Hit Rating cap is 8%, and you must reach this amount to ensure that your attacks do not miss, which can cause you to lose potential damage and Holy Power.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Expertise Rating</b> - The Expertise cap is 6.5%, and you must reach this amount to ensure that your attacks are not dodged, which can cause you to lose potential damage and Holy Power.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Strength</b> - This is our primary stat, one that cannot be reforged, so we will take it wherever we possibly can most of the time. Strength converts into attack power and indirectly spell power.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Mastery</b> - This stat adds additional holy damage to our primary abilities <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=35395/crusader-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_crusaderstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Strike</span></a>, <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=85256/templars-verdict">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_paladin_templarsverdict.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Templar's Verdict</span></a>, and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=53385/divine-storm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_divinestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Storm</span></a>. Once Hit and Expertise caps are reached, this will be our most valuable secondary stat.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Critical Strike Chance</b> - Increases the chance to critically strike. A solid secondary stat, but not the best.</div></li>
<li>
<div data-markup-content-target="1">
<b>Haste</b> - Haste increases the rate at which we attack, but also with <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=25956/sanctity-of-battle">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_sword_136.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Sanctity of Battle</span></a> talented will reduce the cooldown of <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=35395/crusader-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_crusaderstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Strike</span></a> and <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=53385/divine-storm">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/ability_paladin_divinestorm.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Divine Storm</span></a>. That being said, it is our weakest secondary stat and we are unable to reach the point where it will bring <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=35395/crusader-strike">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_crusaderstrike.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Crusader Strike</span></a> cooldown to 3-seconds.</div></li></ol>This is the same order of stat importance when it comes to reforging, excluding Strength which cannot be reforged.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="justice-points">Justice Points for Retribution Paladin DPS Phase 2</h3>None of the items here are pre-raid best in slot, and most of the decent items from Justice Points are easily replaced with better items - thus, spend these points filling in whatever gear you have not obtained from dungeons and reputation rewards.<h3 class="heading-size-3" id="valor-points">Valor Points for Retribution Paladin DPS Phase 2</h3>
<b>The most important items you can buy with <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> is Tier 11 legs, gloves and chest</b>. <br/>Here is my recommended priority for <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> purchases:<br/>
<br/>
