<div class="pad"></div>
<div class="pad"></div>Here we are picking up the Tier 11 legs first <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60347/reinforced-sapphirium-legplates">
<img alt="Reinforced Sapphirium Legplates" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_pants_plate_raidpaladin_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Sapphirium Legplates</span></a> as our first tier item, with the assumption that we will be crafting the <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=55060/elementium-deathplate">
<img alt="Elementium Deathplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Deathplate</span></a>. After legs, you should buy the Tier 11 gloves <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=60345/reinforced-sapphirium-gauntlets">
<img alt="Reinforced Sapphirium Gauntlets" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_gauntlets_plate_raidpaladin_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Reinforced Sapphirium Gauntlets</span></a> and complete the 2-set bonus. Then, for your third purchase, you will want to pick up the Tier 11 chest, waiting to either upgrade it to 372 item level or waiting for helm/<wbr/>shoulders to complete the 4-set bonus before you replace your <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=55060/elementium-deathplate">
<img alt="Elementium Deathplate" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_chest_plate_raidwarrior_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Elementium Deathplate</span></a> with it. <br/>
<br/>Once we have all three Retribution Tier 11 valor pieces, we will pick up the Protection Tier 11 pieces, as we can use this before the pull to extend our <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86150/guardian-of-ancient-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_heroism.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Guardian of Ancient Kings</span></a> duration, swapping back to Retribution gear right before combat begins. It's a little bit try-hard, but offers a significant damage increase during our burst window and can be done painlessly using a macro. Ideally you won't use the tier gloves, as swapping gloves will put your <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=82175/synapse-springs">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> on cooldown, but delaying <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=82175/synapse-springs">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/trade_engineering.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Synapse Springs</span></a> is better than not doing the pre-pull trick at all, so the gloves can be used until you get both shoulders and helm from raid. We will be using this trick for the rest of the expansion. If you do not care to do this pre-pull Protection set <a class="icontiny" data-entity="spell" data-entity-has-icon="true" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/spell=86150/guardian-of-ancient-kings">
<img loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_heroism.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Guardian of Ancient Kings</span></a> extension trick, you can skip these items. This pre-pull maneuver is explained in more detail in the <a href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/guide/classes/paladin/retribution/dps-rotation-cooldowns-abilities-pve">Retribution Rotation Guide</a>.<br/>
<br/>Our next priority after tier is <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=64674/relic-of-aggramar">
<img alt="Relic of Aggramar" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_stone_15.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Relic of Aggramar</span></a> as it is best in slot for Phase 2, and a slight upgrade over <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62243/notched-jawbone">
<img alt="Notched Jawbone" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_jewelry_trinket_06.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Notched Jawbone</span></a> as long as you can use the expertise.<br/>
<br/>Next we will pick up two pre-raid best in slot items: <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58190/floating-web">
<img alt="Floating Web" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_cape_cataclysm_melee_d_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Floating Web</span></a> and <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58185/band-of-bees">
<img alt="Band of Bees" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_pearlring1.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Band of Bees</span></a>. It doesn't matter which order you pick these up, just pick up whatever is the bigger item level upgrade for you first. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58195/woe-breeders-boots">
<img alt="Woe Breeder's Boots" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_raidwarrior_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Woe Breeder's Boots</span></a> is bind-on-equip so instead of paying 1650 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> for them, you can simply buy them on an alt character and mail them to your main, or you can buy them on the auction house instead. These are a low priority purchase due to this, but also because they have zero mastery and are not that much better than <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=62418/boots-of-sullen-rock">
<img alt="Boots of Sullen Rock" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raiddeathknight_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Boots of Sullen Rock</span></a>. If you're going to buy boots from the auction house, the better option is to buy our pre-raid best in slot <a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=59464/treads-of-savage-beatings">
<img alt="Treads of Savage Beatings" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_boots_plate_raiddeathknight_i_01.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Treads of Savage Beatings</span></a>. Due to being bind-on-equip you can get these before your first raid. <br/>
<br/>
<a class="q4 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=58180/license-to-slay">
<img alt="License to Slay" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/inv_misc_note_02.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">License to Slay</span></a> is not really worth buying for the average person as it doesn't even classify as pre-raid best in slot, as it is worse than <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56393/heart-of-solace">
<img alt="Heart of Solace" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_persecution.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Solace</span></a>, so the only reason to get this is if you still do not have <a class="q3 icontiny" data-entity="item" data-entity-has-icon="true" data-game="wow" data-type="item" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/item=56393/heart-of-solace">
<img alt="Heart of Solace" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/spell_holy_persecution.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Heart of Solace</span></a> and have points to spare, having gotten everything else already.<br/>
<br/>The valor points cap increases by 1600 <a class="icontiny q1" data-entity="currency" data-game="wow" data-type="currency" href="https://www.wowhead.com/cata/currency=396/valor-points">
<span>
<img alt="Valor Points" loading="lazy" src="https://wow.zamimg.com/images/wow/icons/tiny/pvecurrency-valor.gif" style="vertical-align: middle;"/> <span class="tinyicontxt">Valor Points</span></span></a> per weekly reset. Due to how the valor point cap works, allowing you to farm all the valor points for previous weeks you may have missed, you can immediately farm as many valor points as you need in order to buy all of the items at this point of the phase, before you even step foot into a raid, so we will include all of them in the set. <br/>
<br/>
